# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark scratch media
#
# The harness allocates real images to measure against - 16/64/256 MB erase and
# verification targets, 32/128 MB carve-scaling images, fragmented and wiped
# fixtures. A full run is well over a gigabyte per output directory. They are
# regenerated by `python -m tools.benchmark`, so only the reports are kept:
# benchmark.json and PERFORMANCE.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/work/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pitch deck
#
# The SIH presentation is a submission deliverable, not source: the template,
# the generated .pptx, the exported PDF and slide PNGs, the diagram and chart
# assets, and the build scripts that produce them. Kept off the remote by
# choice - the same call covers SIH's own template file, which is theirs and
# not something to redistribute.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
deck/
SIH2026-IDEA-Presentation-Format.pptx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state
#
# SANCTUM writes case data, audit chains and exports under its own home
# directory. If one is ever created inside the tree, it must not be committed -
# an audit chain is evidence, and evidence does not belong in a git history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sanctum_home/
cases/
*.log

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
